# Database Rules

- PostgreSQL is the sole primary database; schemas include `core`, `transport`, `rfx`, `documents`, `billing`, and control-tower projections per migrations.
- Migrations live in `infrastructure/migrations/` as numbered `*.up.sql` / `*.down.sql` pairs.
- No destructive schema change without explicit authorization.
- Migrations must be forward-safe and reversible where down files exist.
- Never rewrite already-applied migration history casually.
- Tenant-owned tables require correct tenant isolation (`tenant_id`, scoped indexes, scoped queries).
- Add indexes that support new critical tenant-scoped access patterns.
- Keep migration + model + repository changes synchronized.
- Apply migrations via Makefile (`make migrate-up`, `make migrate-down`, `make migrate-version`); do not run destructive migrate targets without explicit approval.
